# Normalize line endings to LF for everything Git considers text, so
# Windows/Linux/Mac clones all see the same bytes and nobody gets the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning going forward. Git's own
# text/binary auto-detection is generally reliable, but the binary
# extensions below are pinned explicitly rather than left to
# heuristics -- getting this wrong for a real binary (corrupting a
# .wasm by attempting line-ending conversion on it) is a much worse
# failure than a false negative on some obscure text format.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.wasm   binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.xls    binary
*.xlsx   binary
*.zip    binary
*.pem    binary
*.key    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
